        {
          "text": "**Managing File Writing and Git Operations**\n\nThe tool calls should be executed through the safe-output tool, and I can later handle the noop after reviewing the results. My script needs to write the file only if it has changed. Since the instructions say to create or completely replace the `docs/copilot-app-releases.html`, it's fine to go ahead and do that.\n\nSo the sequence goes like this: I’ll write the file first, check for content changes, and if it’s unchanged, I’ll call noop. If there are changes, I’ll create a new git branch named based on the UTC date. I need to ensure that this branch name matches the current git branch, and I will run the necessary Python and git commands in a single bash execution. Time to craft that Python script!",
