          "text": "**Crafting HTML from JSON**\n\nI'm thinking about using Python to load parsed JSON and generate HTML that meets the specified requirements. I need to ensure that any untrusted values are HTML-escaped using `html.escape`. My goal is to facilitate a client-side search across versions, highlights, fixes, and release notes. I’ll summarize concise highlights and fixes based on the content from the release notes body. I’ll look for headings like \"Highlights\" and \"Fixes\" and ensure to handle cases where there might not be any listed highlights or fixes.",
